WEBVTT

c1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Welcome to Treasury Fundamentals. In this session we cover the sub-departments that make up the Treasury and Funds Management function.

c2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:18.000
Treasury & Funds Management has three main sub-departments: Banking, Fund Utilization, and Investments and Corpus Management.

c3
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:28.000
The Banking sub-department handles bank reconciliations, cash handling procedures, and monitors fraud risks across all treasury accounts.

c4
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:38.000
Fund Utilization ensures money is disbursed in advance to each department according to the approved monthly budget.

c5
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:50.000
Investments and Corpus Management maintains proper documentation for 12A and 80G to sustain donor tax incentives and tracks foreign funds separately from domestic donations.

c6
00:00:50.500 --> 00:01:02.000
Risk management is integral to treasury: monitoring fraud risks, ensuring bank reconciliations, controlling cash handling, and maintaining internal financial controls.

c7
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:14.000
The Finance and Accounts department works alongside Treasury for month-end closing, GST filings, and internal financial controls compliance.

c8
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:26.000
Fund raising and donations are a separate but coordinated function. Treasury records inflows; Fund Raising manages donor relationships and campaigns.
